# Day 24 – LEFT JOIN and RIGHT JOIN

## What I Learned
Today I learned about:

- LEFT JOIN → keeps all data from the left table
- RIGHT JOIN → keeps all data from the right table
- How they differ from INNER JOIN
- When to use each JOIN type

LEFT and RIGHT JOIN are used when we want to see unmatched data.

---

## LEFT JOIN

### Definition
LEFT JOIN returns:
- All rows from the left table
- Matching rows from the right table
- NULL if there is no match

### Simple Rule
LEFT JOIN = Keep everything on the LEFT side

---

## LEFT JOIN Syntax

```sql
SELECT column_name
FROM table1
LEFT JOIN table2
ON table1.column_name = table2.column_name;
